      "message": "Downsides to this approach:\n1. SetupInstance semantics return to being unclear (is \u0027Instance\u0027 per thread? Is \u0027Instance\u0027 per process?)\n2. ::get() call is used to instantiate HostConnection from ANGLE path, rather than the ::getOrCreate() call used in the SetupInstance path. This call does not include the kCapsetGfxStreamVulkan used to instantiate the HostConnection on other threads. (Impact unknown, but incorrect per intent.)\n\nUpsides of this approach:\n1. Fewer lines of code changed (ignoring that they\u0027ve already been changed).\n2. rcEnc guaranteed to be created alongside HostConnection, rather than as an ancillary part.\n\nI like #2, but I still feel pretty strongly that the semantics around both SetupInstance and ::get/::getOrCreate need to be refined. I\u0027d personally rather keep the existing code and work to refine those semantics, then fall back to #2 once those have been cleared up?",
